## Reduced-bundle validation (2026-10-22)

- PyInstaller clean build contains 19 Qt6 runtime DLLs, no QML asset tree, and no generic-touch, platform-input-context, or QML-tooling plugin groups. The app bundle contains no expanded attribution HTML; readable notices are generated into the ignored installer staging directory and embedded in the installer.
- The installer was silently installed into a new temporary directory. The installed copy contained the 19 Qt DLLs, 57 Qt attribution pages, all 125 WebEngine/Chromium pages, and the required license texts.
- Launched the installed executable with `PATH` restricted to Windows system directories. The main window appeared, the Steam Workshop tab opened, and the bundled `QtWebEngineProcess.exe` started. Silent uninstall removed the installed executable. The existing app settings registry key was exported before the test and restored byte-for-byte afterward.
- 69 unit tests passed with one environment-only symlink skip; Ruff check, Ruff format check, and compileall passed.
- Installer install/launch/uninstall and restricted-environment behavior were checked in isolated locations on the build host. Windows 10 coverage, the tagged workflow's CPython 3.14 build, and upgrade from a previous version of this optimized installer remain unverified. Real-game global-list apply/launch acceptance was completed on Build 42.21.0; see `docs/PROGRESS.md` for the test and restoration evidence. Gameplay and save-loading behavior were not tested.
